  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting AGYW4 Improved Representation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adolescent girls and young women from underserved and hard to reach communities are often underrepresented in decision making and policy making spheres in Zimbabwe leaving their need unaddressed and their contributions overshadowed.This project seeks to strengthen the capacity of adolescent girls across the 10 provinces of Zimbabwe through various initiatives and activities, engaging them in knowledge development and management ,campaigns to shift the &#x201c;narrative on the politics of representation&#x201d; therefore equipping them with the right and adequate skill sets to effectively and efficiently represent and participate in all stages of policy making ensuring that their inputs are incorporated into all policies that matter to them . The methodology which willbe used to achieve the desired goals is through participation drawn from the feminist principles of inclusivity,collective action and equality .Ultimately thisproject provides a platform that will ensure an increase in representation and participation ofthe adolescent girls and young womenin policy and decision-making spaces in Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="23">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development Agenda for Girls and Wo</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development Agenda for Girls and Women in Africa Network (DAWA) is an indigenous, community based , girl and young women founded and led feminist network in Africa,based in Zimbabwe. DAWA seeks to collaborate with marginalised girls and young women (15 to 35 years) to promote their rights, leadership and representation in decision making spaces and processes. We co-create spaces to engage in much needed advocacy on a myriad of issues. To date, DAWA has over 600+ girls and young women individual members across Eastern and Southern Africa, 189 individuals in Zimbabwe , 62 member organisations and 45 out 62 are girl and young women-led organisations . Weare passionate to drive the social development changes in our communities as we bring together our livedexperiences to change development outcomes.

Our vision is to achieve a future where girls and young women have control over the resources they need and the power to use them to end inequalities and fulfil their rights.

Our mission is to become the leading network in East and Southern Africa that enables adolescent girls and young women leaders to self-organise for social good.

Our strategy to achieve our vision and mission includes intersectional feminist movement building, advocacy, feminist accompaniment, accountability, capacity strengthening and knowledge management. Our collaborations and work is deeply rooted in equality,integrity,innovation, collaboration, accountability and accompaniment which are our key values.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
